# Push after every change

When the user asks for any code, rates, or portal change, finish by committing the relevant files and pushing to `origin` on the current branch (usually `main`).

- Do this without waiting to be asked again.
- Do not include `.env`, credentials, or unrelated untracked files.
- Do not include `.cursor/` unless the change is a rule they asked for.
- Use a short commit message that says why the change was made.
- After push, mention that Netlify will pick up `main`.
